subsys/pmci/pldm/serial_bridge: add a RISC-V RERI RAS handler

Add the firmware side of the RISC-V RERI (RAS Error-record Register Interface,
v1.0) hardware-fault -> BMC reporting path to the PLDM serial_bridge sample.
It pairs with the RERI error-injection shell (patch 0013) and the QEMU RERI
error-bank device (patch 0012).

On the abstract RERI RAS signal (delivered here as a PLIC interrupt, source 50,
from the QEMU RERI device), the handler walks the bank the architected way:
read valid_summary, then for each valid record read status_i / addr_info_i,
classify the error severity, latch it, and clear status_i.v via control_i.sinv.
The RERI RAS signal is level-based -- the modelled hardware holds the line
asserted while any record has status_i.v == 1 -- so the handler must sinv to
drop the interrupt, which it does on every serviced record.

The latched severity is exposed to the BMC as a PLDM Type 2 numeric sensor
(sensor id 2); the BMC's platform-mc discovers it from the PDR and polls it
with GetSensorReading, so the injected hardware fault is observed over PLDM
without the firmware pushing an event from interrupt context (the PLDM TX path
is not ISR-safe). This is the only Type 2 path with a live per-poll callback,
hence the RAS state rides on a numeric sensor rather than a state sensor.

Interrupt binding is deliberately isolated in reri_ras_init(): the RAS
decode/report body reads only architected RERI registers, so moving from a
PLIC external interrupt to an AIA local interrupt (RERI high/low RAS signals
-> local IRQ 43/35) would change only the IRQ_CONNECT glue, not the reporting
logic.

Changes
  * src/reri_ras.c (new)
      RAS ISR (valid_summary walk, severity latch, sinv acknowledge) + the
      PLDM numeric-sensor read callback + reri_ras_init() (IRQ_CONNECT on
      DT_IRQN(reri0)) + reri_ras_register_sensor().
  * src/reri_ras.h (new)
      RAS handler interface (init / register_sensor / get_event /
      severity_now, struct reri_ras_event).
  * src/main.c
      register the RAS sensor before the Type 2 responder and call
      reri_ras_init() after the responder is up.
  * CMakeLists.txt
      build src/reri_ras.c.

Verified: builds clean for hifive_unleashed/fu540/u54 (Zephyr v4.3.0, SDK
0.17.4); reri_ras_init / reri_ras_isr / reri_ras_register_sensor are present
in the ELF and the RAS sensor is added to the Type 2 PDR repository.
